warning: `table.insert` with index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(t, 0, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: did you mean index 1?

warning: `table.insert` with index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(t, 0x0, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: did you mean index 1?

warning: `table.remove` with index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.remove(t, 0x0)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: did you mean index 1?

warning: `table.move` with start index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.move(t, 0x0, #t, 1)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

warning: `table.move` with destination index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.move(t, 1, #t, 0x0, u)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

warning: `table.insert(t, #t + 1, v)` appends, so the index argument is redundant
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(t, #t + 0x1, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: use `table.insert(t, v)` instead

warning: `table.remove(t, #t - 1)` removes the value before the last element
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.remove(t, #t - 0x1)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: `table.remove(t)` removes the last element

warning: `table.insert(t, #t, v)` inserts the value before the last element
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(t, #t, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: to append, use `table.insert(t, v)`

warning: `table.insert(t, #t + 1, v)` appends, so the index argument is redundant
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(t, #t + 1, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: use `table.insert(t, v)` instead

warning: `table.insert(t, #t, v)` inserts the value before the last element
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.insert(a.b, #a.b, v)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: to append, use `table.insert(t, v)`

warning: `table.remove` with index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.remove(t, 0)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: did you mean index 1?

warning: `table.remove(t, #t - 1)` removes the value before the last element
 --> Lua54:1:1
1 | table.remove(t, #t - 1)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
help: `table.remove(t)` removes the last element

warning: `table.move` with start index 0, but Lua arrays are 1-based
